.TH KWYBARS 1 "October 2026" "Kwybars 0.3.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
kwybars \- audio visualizer overlay for Wayland desktops
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B kwybars
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ command ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B kwybars
draws real-time audio bars directly on the desktop, usually anchored to a
screen edge. It captures what plays on the default PipeWire output, shows
the bars when audio starts, and hides them when it stops. While nothing
plays it draws nothing and does no work.
.PP
Without a command,
.B kwybars
runs the visualizer until it is stopped. With a command it checks the setup
or changes a config file, then exits.
.PP
It needs a Wayland compositor that supports the layer-shell protocol, and
PipeWire.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-c,\ \-\-config\  PATH
Use the config at
.I PATH
instead of the default location. Works with every command.
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Print help and exit.
.TP
.B \-V, \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B validate\-config
Check the config file, the adjacent
.IR colors.toml ,
the configured theme, and the overlay image, the same way the visualizer
reads them. Unknown, removed, and out-of-range keys are warnings.
.TP
.B doctor
Print the same report as
.BR validate\-config ,
then check the Wayland connection, layer-shell and fractional-scale support,
every monitor and whether the config puts the visualizer on it, PipeWire,
whether the
.I kwybars.service
user unit is enabled, and where the log file is.
.TP
.B list\-themes
List the themes the config can name and where each one comes from.
.TP
.BI switch\-config\  FILE
Replace the config path with a symbolic link to
.IR FILE ,
in one step, so a running
.B kwybars
switches to it. A regular file at the config path is first copied to
.IR name.bak .
The config path is the one given by
.BR \-\-config ,
or
.B \-a, \-\-active
as another spelling of it.
.TP
.BI image\-overlay\ match\ \-\-overlay\-dir\  DIR\ WALLPAPER
Find the image in
.I DIR
that has the same file name as
.I WALLPAPER
with the extension
.IR png ,
.IR webp ,
.IR jpg ,
or
.IR jpeg ,
in that order, and set
.B [image_overlay] enabled
and
.B path
in the config. The rest of the file is left as written. If the config path
is a symbolic link to a file inside the link's directory, that file is
edited.
.TP
.B debug audio
Show a live level meter of the captured audio in the terminal.
.TP
.B debug spectrum
Show the analyzed bars in the terminal.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success. For the checking commands: no error was found.
.TP
.B 1
The visualizer could not start or lost the compositor, a checking command
found an error, or a config command failed.
.TP
.B 2
The command line was not understood.
.SH CONFIGURATION
The config file is TOML. Its path is the first of:
.IP "1." 4
.BI \-\-config\  PATH
.IP "2." 4
.B $KWYBARS_CONFIG
.IP "3." 4
.B $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/kwybars/config.toml
.IP "4." 4
.B $HOME/.config/kwybars/config.toml
.PP
If no config exists, built-in defaults are used. The sections are
.BR [overlay] ,
.BR [visualizer] ,
.BR [image_overlay] ,
.BR [activity] ,
and
.BR [audio] .
The full reference is at
.UR https://naurissteins.com/kwybars
.UE .
.PP
The config,
.IR colors.toml ,
the theme file, and the overlay image are watched and reloaded while
.B kwybars
runs. A config that fails to load leaves the running one active, and the
error is written to the log.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/kwybars/config.toml
Default user configuration file.
.TP
.I ~/.config/kwybars/colors.toml
Optional color overrides, read from beside the config file.
.TP
.I ~/.config/kwybars/themes/
User theme directory.
.TP
.I /usr/share/kwybars/themes/
Packaged copies of the built-in themes.
.TP
.I /usr/share/doc/kwybars/examples/
Packaged example configurations.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/systemd/user/kwybars.service
Packaged user service.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/kwybars/kwybars.log
Default log file when
.B XDG_STATE_HOME
is unset.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B KWYBARS_CONFIG
Config path used when
.B \-\-config
is not given.
.TP
.B KWYBARS_THEMES_DIR
Extra theme directories, separated by colons.
.TP
.B KWYBARS_LOG
Log level or filter, for example
.BR debug .
Falls back to
.B RUST_LOG
when unset.
.TP
.B KWYBARS_LOG_FILE
Log file path.
.TP
.B WAYLAND_DISPLAY
The Wayland display to connect to.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Run the visualizer:
.B kwybars
.TP
Run with an explicit config:
.B kwybars \-\-config ~/.config/kwybars/current.toml
.TP
Find out why nothing shows:
.B kwybars doctor
.TP
Check a config:
.B kwybars validate\-config \-\-config ~/.config/kwybars/custom/wave.toml
.TP
Switch the running visualizer to another preset:
.B kwybars switch\-config ~/.config/kwybars/custom/wave.toml
.TP
Match a wallpaper to an image overlay:
.B kwybars image\-overlay match \-\-overlay\-dir ~/.config/kwybars/overlays ~/Pictures/wallpapers/forest.jpg
.TP
Enable the user service:
.B systemctl \-\-user enable \-\-now kwybars.service
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR pipewire (1)
